# Copy to .env.sourcing-agent next to docker-compose.sourcing-agent.yml, in /srv/agents/sourcing-agent (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The env file"). The copy has mode 600 on the host.
# Names, placeholders and published values only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token.
# The service and the runtime both read this file, and no other. A name that the compose file sets wins over this file, so none of those names stands here. Three kinds of line are the exception: the window of the advert, which both sides read, the supplier key line, which the service blanks, and the nine key lines of the service, which the runtime blanks.
# The copy holds ten keys and a token. It never enters git: the .gitignore of the repository covers .env.* except *.example.
# A container reads this file when it is created. After a change, create the container again: restart does not read it (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The restart rule").
# A value that breaks a rule stops the start of the service, and the error names the variable and never shows the value.
# The supplier key of the runtime. The runtime signs its receipts with it, and its wallet sits at SUPPLIER_ADDRESS. The service never holds it: the compose file blanks SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX for the service.
# The service reads the two public lines, SUPPLIER_PKH and SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX, and publishes them in its manifest. SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX is the public key, 64 hex characters. SUPPLIER_PKH is its hash, 56 hex characters.
# All four lines are empty here on purpose. Write each one with a command that prints nothing, and never type a key in a shell (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The env file").
SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PKH=
SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# The nine keys of the service. Each one is a raw Ed25519 key of 64 lowercase hex characters, and each one is a key of its own: the service stops at start when two keys are equal, or when a key is the supplier key.
# SOURCING_SERVICE is the service key. It pays the model hires, signs the claim and the challenges, and signs the subject token of the agent. The service files the challenges and signs the token. An operator command makes the stake and the claim with this key, and the service never does.
# SOURCING_DELEGATION_1 and SOURCING_DELEGATION_2 are the delegation keys. The delegation of a hirer names one of them. The key pays the quote hires, and it signs the vault payment, the Accept and the sub-delegations of a job: up to three, one for each scorer.
# SCORER_1_AUTH and SCORER_1_DELEGATION, SCORER_2_AUTH and SCORER_2_DELEGATION, SCORER_3_AUTH and SCORER_3_DELEGATION are the two keys of each of the three subagents scorer-1 to scorer-3: an authentication key and a delegation key. A scorer holds no funds of its own: the wallet of the delegation key of the job pays its Delegate.
# Each key has a key hash line, PKH, after it. The line is public and optional. When it has a value, it must be the hash of the key before it, or the service stops at start.
# All eighteen lines are empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without its keys. The compose file blanks the nine key lines for the runtime.
SOURCING_SERVICE_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SOURCING_SERVICE_PKH=
SOURCING_DELEGATION_1_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SOURCING_DELEGATION_1_PKH=
SOURCING_DELEGATION_2_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SOURCING_DELEGATION_2_PKH=
SCORER_1_AUTH_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_1_AUTH_PKH=
SCORER_1_DELEGATION_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_1_DELEGATION_PKH=
SCORER_2_AUTH_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_2_AUTH_PKH=
SCORER_2_DELEGATION_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_2_DELEGATION_PKH=
SCORER_3_AUTH_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_3_AUTH_PKH=
SCORER_3_DELEGATION_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SCORER_3_DELEGATION_PKH=
# The token between the runtime and the service. The runtime sends this value, as it stands, as the authorization header of every call to the service. The service answers POST / and POST /precheck only to a call that carries it.
# The form is "Bearer <64 hex characters>", with the quotes: the value has a space. Docker Compose takes the quotes off. The runtime and the service read this one line, so they hold one value.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it, so a step that was forgotten cannot leave a service that answers anyone. The value stays in this file. Never paste it into a chat or a log.
SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER=""
# The chain. The runtime reads these lines. They hold public values of Vector mainnet: the network, the node, the time of slot 0, and the reference scripts of the legacy escrow and the legacy advert.
# LIVE_CHAIN=1 lets the runtime write to the chain, and the release watcher needs it. Keep ESCROW_REF_UTXO and ADVERT_REF_UTXO while legacy escrows exist.
NETWORK_ID=1
OGMIOS_URL=https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_ZERO_TIME_MS=1756485600000
LIVE_CHAIN=1
ESCROW_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#0
ADVERT_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#1
# The identity registry deployment. The lines hold the values that the deployment on Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03.
# The runtime works an escrow that names the agent with IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, the two scripts IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO, and AGENT_ID.
# The service reads the four VECTOR_IDENTITY lines for the escrows that it posts and the vault payments that it builds. VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT is the Merkle root of the adoption allowlist, and VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED is the output of the seal of the configuration.
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO are the reference scripts of the escrow and of the vault. IDENTITY_POLICY_ID must be the policy that the root and the output give, or the service stops at start and names the variables.
IDENTITY_POLICY_ID=d958b823faaa76977d0a07bd9622e87d8e2c85f6692f7f8e8db77762
IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO=5efd18a1d90a6b87f1fd4b6fe93acfbe5be082260fd52be194b1088ade7c2758#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT=e4b6b17ce4a8f83aa17d3181ea140d2bd76c0cfa8a7c44ad69543800b4a0df01
VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED=6c9856c70b1101f1a4e9ceb373188608013416eff48c51f5bb62706a65d41a2a#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO=d0bf8f73c915fcbf57ddba714256e520a9a0820bc9e643218db8cf54762d215b#0
# IDENTITY_ADDRESS is the address of the identity registry. Empty means the address of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, which is right here.
IDENTITY_ADDRESS=
# The record and the advert of the agent. AGENT_ID is the identifier of the agent record: 64 hex characters, the part of AGENT_DID after did:vector:. ADVERT_REF is the reference of the advert: <transaction hash>#<output index>.
# Both lines are empty here on purpose. The operator posts the advert with the hosted tools after the service runs, and writes both values here (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The start order"). The runtime does not start without ADVERT_REF.
AGENT_ID=
ADVERT_REF=
# The Module-1 deployment manifest. The dispute code reads it at start: a challenge needs its scripts and its parameters. It is an https address pinned to one commit of the repository of the Module-1 deployment.
# Replace the placeholder <commit> with the 40 hex digits of the commit that the hosted MCP server uses for its own VECTOR_MODULE1_MANIFEST (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The env file"). The manifest at that commit must be the one of the identity registry of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID.
VECTOR_MODULE1_MANIFEST=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Apex-Fusion/vector-agent-modules/<commit>/Module-1/deploy/identity/mainnet/manifest.json
# The services that the checks, the hires and the dispute code read. Each line is empty here, and an empty line keeps the default of the code, which is Vector mainnet. Set a line only to use another service.
# VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL is the node, and the code takes an https address only: the janitor reads the tip of the node with it. VECTOR_KOIOS_URL is the indexer of the ledger. VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL takes the transactions.
# VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL is the marketplace indexer, in which the agent finds the Bid Desks. IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL is the identity gateway.
VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL=
VECTOR_KOIOS_URL=
VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL=
VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL=
IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL=
# The two hosts of the mock systems (deploy/server/README.md, "The two mock host names"). Both are required. Each value is an https origin: https://, one host name, and no path. The two must be two different hosts.
# MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE is the host of tokens, where the scorers read the vendor master and where the service writes the approved ranking. MOCK_MTLS_BASE is the client-certificate host. Each value must name the same host as its block in the Caddy file of the mock systems.
MOCK_PUBLIC_BASE=<https origin of the mock host>
MOCK_MTLS_BASE=<https origin of the mock mtls host>
# The issuer of the compliance attestations that the agent counts: the compliance registry. COMPLIANCE_ISSUER_PKH is its key hash, a public value of 56 hex characters, and the manifest names it. An attestation of any other issuer is not counted.
# The placeholder stays until the operator knows the key hash of the compliance registry. The service stops at start without a value.
COMPLIANCE_ISSUER_PKH=<key hash of the compliance registry>
# The three scorers. Each one is a subagent with an agent record of its own, and this agent is its parent. The three lines hold the DIDs of the three records: did:vector: and the 64 hex characters of each record. All three are required.
# No scorer is this agent, and no two scorers are one agent. The lines are empty here on purpose: the DIDs exist after the records are made (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The env file").
SCORER_1_DID=
SCORER_2_DID=
SCORER_3_DID=
# The terms of the advert, as the service publishes them in its manifest. The price is 3 units, 3000000 lovelace. Each bond is 1 unit and is fixed in the code. The lock of the escrow is the price and both bonds: 5 units.
# The window is in milliseconds: 90 minutes. The compose file gives the runtime the same value, and the service does not start with less than 5400000. The operator posts the advert with these terms (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The start order").
ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE=3000000
ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS=5400000
# The manifest. What the service serves at /agent.json is hashed into the advert, so each line that goes into it must be final before the hash is taken: OPERATOR_CONTACT, AGENT_DID, AGENT_VERSION, AGENT_STATUS_CHIP, AGENT_STATUS_SINCE and ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL of this block; ADVERT_PRICE_LOVELACE and ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS, the terms of the advert; COMPLIANCE_ISSUER_PKH, the issuer of the compliance attestations; IDENTITY_POLICY_ID and IDENTITY_ADDRESS, the identity registry; SUPPLIER_PKH and SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX, the supplier lines; SOURCING_SERVICE_PKH, SOURCING_DELEGATION_1_PKH and SOURCING_DELEGATION_2_PKH, the key hashes of the three paying keys; and LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST and LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE, the model and the price limit of the model hire.
# The three scorers, the keys of the scorers, the other limits of the hires, the co-sign lines and the dispute lines are not in the manifest: a change of them leaves the hash as it is. A change of a line above means a retired advert and a new one. OPERATOR_CONTACT is required and is published. Write the role address that the operator confirms, never the address of a person.
# AGENT_DID is written when the agent record exists: did:vector: and the 64 hex characters of the agent identifier. It is required. AGENT_VERSION stays empty: the service has its own default.
# AGENT_STATUS_CHIP is proposed, deployed or live, and it stays proposed until the first live run. Empty AGENT_STATUS_SINCE keeps the default date of the code, and a date as YYYY-MM-DD goes with a change of the word.
# ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL stays empty: the transaction of an advert cannot be inside the manifest that the advert hashes.
OPERATOR_CONTACT=<role address of the operator>
AGENT_DID=
AGENT_VERSION=
AGENT_STATUS_CHIP=proposed
AGENT_STATUS_SINCE=
ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL=
# What the service hires. The first four lines limit the model hire of its decisions: the models, comma separated with no space, in order of preference, and the most that a hire may be priced at, 1000000 lovelace, 1 unit.
# The two bond lines of the model limit the supplier bond and the buyer bond of the model advert. Every such advert has bonds of 1000000, so 2000000 is the limit for each. These are the values of Advocate.
# The last three lines limit the hire of a quote from a Bid Desk: the advert of a Bid Desk costs 1 unit and has bonds of 1 unit, so 2000000 lovelace is the limit for the price and for each bond, twice what the advert asks. The delegation of the hirer limits each payment too.
# All seven lines are required, and the service never fills in a limit for you.
LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=1000000
LLM_MAX_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
LLM_MAX_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
QUOTE_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=2000000
QUOTE_MAX_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
QUOTE_MAX_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
# The co-sign route, POST /cosign/delegate. It needs no token, so the allowlist decides who may ask. COSIGN_ALLOWLIST is required: the key hashes (56 lowercase hex characters) of the principals whose delegation the route may co-sign, separated by commas.
# The empty value holds nobody, and the route then signs for nobody. The line is empty here on purpose. A change needs a new service container (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The restart rule").
# The three limits are optional. An empty line keeps the default of the kit: 4 calls at one time, one hour for the furthest end of the validity window of a transaction, and 5000 ms for one read of the ledger.
COSIGN_ALLOWLIST=
COSIGN_MAX_CONCURRENT=
COSIGN_MAX_FUTURE_MS=
COSIGN_LEDGER_TIMEOUT_MS=
# The dispute code. The stake of a challenge, in lovelace: the Module-1 deployment on Vector mainnet asks at least 50000000 for a claim, and a challenge targets a claim whose stake is not above this value. So this is the least stake.
# DISPUTE_MIN_WINDOW_LEFT_MS is the least time that a claim must still have in its challenge window: 600000, 10 minutes. DISPUTE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS is the most time that one read of the dispute code may take: 20000, and the code takes 30000 at most.
# The last two lines are optional and empty. The dispute code takes the resolution deadline from the Module-1 deployment, and a value here must be equal to it. A lease is how long an unfinished challenge blocks a second try for its escrow.
DISPUTE_CHALLENGE_STAKE_LOVELACE=50000000
DISPUTE_MIN_WINDOW_LEFT_MS=600000
DISPUTE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
DISPUTE_RESOLUTION_DEADLINE_MS=
DISPUTE_STARTED_LEASE_MS=
# The fault switch of the service. The line is empty for a clean run. The one value of this agent is invert_scores, and it is for a failure run only (RUNBOOK-sourcing-agent.md, "The fault switch"): any other value stops the start.
# Every result carries the member fault_mode. It is the empty text in a clean run, and it is the value of the switch in a failure run.
FAULT_MODE=
